  "note": "Example API response for the acceptance test room. All numbers except reason, recommendedAction and commentary are computed by code; those three are written by the AI and must not change any number. safetyScore is rawSafetyScore rounded. fallDirection.axis is used for coordinate calculations. Every item has before and after; for an item that does not move, after = before. displacement.d is the normalized 0-1 displacement of each item (null for items excluded from sliding: bed, door, cable, extinguisher). Every item has impact: hit says whether the item's fall footprint touches any critical zone, hitZones lists the types of those zones (criticalZones[].type: bed, work_area; never exit) and multiplier is the item's impact multiplier, computed by code (cem/kayma_skoru/carpan_hesapla.py: height >= 180 cm -> 1.0, 120-180 -> 0.7, < 120 -> 0.4, x 1.3 for mirror / glass), so the request only needs hit and hitZones; when hit is false, multiplier is null and hitZones is empty. penalties.impacts is computed from impact and criticalZones: each zone type is penalized at most once, by the item or falling load (loads[], multiplier 0.4) with the largest multiplier, points = penaltyPoints x multiplier. The exit penalty is not an impact: it comes from the R4 width check and is written to penalties.impacts with zone exit and rule R4. Each penalties.impacts entry has a rule. When after.pose.position is present it is used as the item's center after shaking. Risk level is 1-5; riskScore is likelihood x severity (1-25). Item type names must exactly match cem/kayma_skoru/esya_tipleri.py."
